Package: conductoR
Title: Perform a Contract-Typed Analytical Plan Across Analytics Components
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Max",
           family = "Moldovan",
           email = "max.moldovan@adelaide.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9680-8474"))
Description: Declares an analytical plan as a directed acyclic graph of
    nodes, each bound to a tool that returns an 'orchestraManifest' result,
    and performs it in topological order. Every edge is typed by the
    inferential target the upstream node declares, and a mismatched handoff
    stops the run before the downstream node executes rather than coercing
    across a contract boundary. Two epistemic operators are built in: a
    power-aware abstention gate that refuses to pass a null verdict the
    design could not have resolved, and a triangulation operator that
    reconciles any number of independent lenses on one question. A plan
    serialises to 'YAML' and back, compiles to a 'targets' pipeline, and
    every run writes a provenance record with the integrity chain of the
    manifests it produced.
